1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,892
Day 51: minimind, an open source pipeline that trains a 64M

2
00:00:05,892 --> 00:00:09,787
parameter LLM from scratch, run on CPU.

3
00:00:10,237 --> 00:00:14,165
minimind implements the full training pipeline, tokenizer,

4
00:00:14,165 --> 00:00:17,755
pretraining, fine tuning, and reinforcement learning,

5
00:00:17,755 --> 00:00:20,802
in pure PyTorch, with no high level wrappers.

6
00:00:21,252 --> 00:00:25,397
We sliced the official dataset down to under half a percent,

7
00:00:25,397 --> 00:00:29,542
and ran the stock pretrain script on four CPU cores, no GPU.

8
00:00:29,992 --> 00:00:32,925
The SFT script loaded that checkpoint and

9
00:00:32,925 --> 00:00:36,216
kept training on a small set of chat examples,

10
00:00:36,216 --> 00:00:37,503
still on CPU only.

11
00:00:37,953 --> 00:00:41,603
We then generated from both checkpoints with the same seed,

12
00:00:41,603 --> 00:00:45,005
comparing raw text continuation against fine-tuned chat

13
00:00:45,005 --> 00:00:45,500
replies.

14
00:00:45,950 --> 00:00:50,166
Pretrain loss dropped from seven point four to four point one

15
00:00:50,166 --> 00:00:52,654
over one thousand six hundred steps.

16
00:00:52,654 --> 00:00:56,456
After SFT, the model gave a coherent self-introduction,

17
00:00:56,456 --> 00:00:59,220
but factual questions stayed incoherent.

18
00:00:59,670 --> 00:01:04,050
Full logs and code are on GitHub, Apache-2.0 licensed.

19
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:05,835
Write-up linked below.
